01. Public vs Private Subnet

This is one of the most important concepts.

Public subnet

A subnet is considered public when its route table has a route to an Internet Gateway.

Example:

Public Subnet
10.0.1.0/24

Route table:

0.0.0.0/0 ---> Internet Gateway

Typical resources:

Internet
   |
   v
ALB
   |
Public Subnet
Private subnet

A private subnet doesn't have a direct route to an Internet Gateway.

Example:

Private Subnet
10.0.10.0/24

Route:
0.0.0.0/0 ---> NAT Gateway

Typical resources:

Application servers
EKS worker nodes
Jenkins agents
Internal services



